ord from 1951 to 2025 shows May to June came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids. In 2025 the middle of the grids ran 125% of normal in June to July, then 58% of normal in August to September. So far in 2026, April to May and May to June each came in at 161% of normal on the middle of the grids. Grid 12154 had its driest year in 2011 at 65% of normal.</p>"}
